{"id": "EUVD-2026-102343", "enisaUuid": "19328d3d-9044-3a5d-8a4f-e42d93fcc930", "description": "Netgate pfSense CE through 2.9.0 contains an authorization bypass vulnerability that allows read-only WebGUI users to replace config.xml because config_restore() and config_install() ignore the 'User - Config: Deny Config Write' privilege. Attackers holding page privileges for services_acb.php, uploadconfig.php, diag_confbak.php, or diag_backup.php can install a chosen config.xml to gain root-level code execution after reload or reboot.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T18:46:31", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T18:46:31", "baseScore": 8.6, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:H/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/abraxas/pfsense-config-readonly-restore", "https://abraxaslabs.tech/research/pfsense-ce-leftovers", "https://github.com/pfsense/pfsense/blob/9363ac5b8651a1c7a333180425ce7719070f95f9/src/etc/inc/config.lib.inc#L743-L798", "https://github.com/pfsense/pfsense/blob/9363ac5b8651a1c7a333180425ce7719070f95f9/src/etc/inc/config.lib.inc#L588-L597", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/netgate-pfsense-ce-through-2.9.0-authorization-bypass-via-config-restore-and-config-install"], "aliases": ["GHSA-prh2-rh73-jcp7", "CVE-2026-111231"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.83, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "f85f7ece-a84e-399c-b9c3-f1f0a00988ce", "product": {"name": "pfSense CE", "vendor": {"name": "Netgate"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22642.9.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "2655fb92-8578-3499-9372-2ddae5d33a6b", "vendor": {"name": "Netgate"}}], "isExploited": false}